IntroduceStudent: {"title": "The Hidden Treasure of Willow Creek", "story": "On a warm June afternoon, twelve\u2011year\u2011old Milo dug in the soft earth behind his house, searching for the baseball his dad had tossed years ago. The garden tangled marigolds, a rusted swing set, and a stone wall that once marked his grandparents\u2019 farm. When his shovel struck something hard, a low hum rose, and a faint blue light seeped through a crack in the wall.\n\nMilo brushed away the dirt and uncovered a smooth, oval stone that pulsed like a heartbeat. He lifted it, and the stone split open, revealing a swirling vortex of silver mist. A cool wind brushed his face, and a whisper floated out, \u201cEnter, if you dare.\u201d His heart hammered, but curiosity won. He stepped forward, and the world behind him dissolved into a bright whirl of colors.\n\nHe emerged in a forest of crystal trees whose leaves chimed like glass bells. A river of liquid light flowed nearby, and floating above it was a unicorn with a mane of starlight. The unicorn bowed its head, and a tiny voice sang, \u201cWelcome, seeker.\u201d Milo gasped. \u201cWhere am I?\u201d he asked, his voice trembling.\n\nA mischievous pixie fluttered from behind a mushroom and landed on his shoulder. \u201cYou\u2019re in Eldoria,\u201d she giggled, \u201cthe realm of forgotten spells.\u201d She pointed to a floating island where a massive ancient spellbook rested on an amber pedestal. The cover shimmered with shifting runes. \u201cThat is the Grimoire of Dawn,\u201d the pixie said, \u201cit grants a single wish to any brave heart.\u201d\n\nMilo\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cCan I\u2026 use it?\u201d he asked.\n\nThe unicorn stepped forward, its horn glowing. \u201cOnly if you prove your worth,\u201d it said. \u201cFirst, you must calm the storm dragon that roams the northern cliffs.\u201d A distant roar echoed, and dark clouds swirled, forming the silhouette of a massive dragon with midnight thunder scales.\n\nMilo felt fear, but the pixie whispered, \u201cRemember the stone you carry; it holds the power of the earth.\u201d He clenched the stone, and it warmed, sending a tremor through his feet. He ran toward the cliffs, the river of light guiding his path. When the dragon appeared, its eyes flashed with ancient fire. Milo raised the stone, and a gentle green glow wrapped the beast in emerald vines. The roar softened, and the dragon lowered its head in peace.\n\nThe unicorn bowed again, and the sky cleared. \u201cYou have shown courage and kindness,\u201d it said. \u201cThe Grimoire of Dawn is yours.\u201d Milo opened the massive book, and a single line glowed: \u201cReturn home, and remember that magic lives wherever wonder persists.\u201d\n\nMilo stepped back through the vortex, feeling the stone dissolve into dust as the portal closed. He found himself in his backyard, the sun setting behind the stone wall. He looked at his hands\u2014dusty, but empty. He smiled, knowing the adventure had changed him. He whispered to the wind, \u201cI will never stop believing.\u201d As the first stars appeared, a faint chime echoed from the marigolds, as if crystal trees sang from afar."}
